{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["And after he mentioned the consecrated offerings of the children of Israel, he warned that they must not bring offerings from animals with blemishes." "And the meaning of <b>and from the ger.</b> is that there is one rule for the one who vows and for the one who voluntarily offers, for Israel and for the ger, for thus it is written. And the Sages distinguished between a vow and a voluntary gift: every vow is a voluntary gift, but not every voluntary gift is a vow. And every offering that goes up entirely on the altar is fit to be without blemish."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:11:44.089071644Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}